diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index b5fe1b2a4feac926b16f4b55fd72f2bb6eb7b711..fd381e32ed452931199266c58702d4c97324e2c8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,25 @@
 The Lakeside Windsurf School teaches windsurfing on the lake from April to October, and rents boards and
 sails to its students and to visitors who bring their own experience. This repository holds the software
 of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
+
+## Rental service
+
+`createRentalService()` creates an isolated, in-memory rental service. Add boards or sails with an
+integer-cent `dailyPrice`, then call `quote` or `book` with UTC ISO-8601 timestamps. Rental periods are
+half-open whole-day intervals: both timestamps must be midnight UTC and `end` is the start of the day
+after the final rental day. A booking rejects an overlapping booking for the same item, while an adjacent
+one is allowed. Cancellation is not yet implemented.
+
+```ts
+import { createRentalService } from './src/index.js';
+
+const rentals = createRentalService();
+rentals.addEquipment({ id: 'board-17', kind: 'board', dailyPrice: 2_500 });
+
+rentals.quote({
+  itemId: 'board-17',
+  start: '2026-06-01T00:00:00Z',
+  end: '2026-06-03T00:00:00Z',
+});
+// { itemId: 'board-17', start: '2026-06-01T00:00:00Z', end: '2026-06-03T00:00:00Z', total: 5000 }
+```
diff --git a/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-001-use-half-open-utc-day-intervals-and-sequential-booking-ids.md b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-001-use-half-open-utc-day-intervals-and-sequential-booking-ids.md
