index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f06b06cc00457753bfde4f3b59b8fefb7c1dd4eb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-001-use-half-open-utc-day-intervals-and-sequential-booking-ids.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-use-half-open-utc-day-intervals-and-sequential-booking-ids
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use half-open UTC day intervals and sequential booking IDs"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The rental module must price full UTC-day periods, prevent overlapping bookings, and create booking
+identifiers without relying on time or randomness.
+
+## Decision
+
+Represent a rental period as a half-open interval `[start, end)`, where both boundaries are UTC
+midnights and `end` is later than `start`. Two bookings overlap when each starts before the other
+ends. Generate booking identifiers sequentially within each service instance, beginning at
+`booking-1`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Adjacent periods can be booked because one ends exactly when the next starts. Pricing is the UTC-day
+count multiplied by the integer-cent daily price. Booking IDs are deterministic in the in-memory
+service and reset when a new service is created.
